WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.113
An antibody-drug conjugate is a chemical system.

00:00:04.113 --> 00:00:04.558
Tumour

00:00:04.558 --> 00:00:08.274
binding is only one step in an exposure and release

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:08.857
problem.

00:00:13.508 --> 00:00:16.888
Stable, cleavable and non-cleavable linkers change

00:00:16.888 --> 00:00:17.158
what

00:00:17.158 --> 00:00:20.605
escapes the carrier, how much reaches other tissues

00:00:20.605 --> 00:00:20.808
and

00:00:20.808 --> 00:00:22.401
how a tumour is exposed.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.740
Drug-to-antibody ratio influences distribution,

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.688
heterogeneity and pharmacokinetics. Higher loading is

00:00:34.688 --> 00:00:34.912
not

00:00:34.912 --> 00:00:36.888
automatically more precise.

00:00:42.092 --> 00:00:45.464
Even a stable linker may deliver a drug class

00:00:45.464 --> 00:00:46.213
associated

00:00:46.213 --> 00:00:49.434
with specific toxicities, including serious

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:50.408
complications

00:00:50.408 --> 00:00:51.806
outside the tumour.

00:00:57.008 --> 00:01:00.230
Permeable payloads may help reach heterogeneous

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:00.779
tumours,

00:01:00.779 --> 00:01:04.343
but surrounding normal tissue and exposure constrain

00:01:04.343 --> 00:01:04.549
the

00:01:04.549 --> 00:01:05.828
apparent advantage.

00:01:10.675 --> 00:01:14.345
The article argues that conjugation chemistry, payload

00:01:14.345 --> 00:01:18.011
choice and predictive toxicology belong together from

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:18.219
the

00:01:18.219 --> 00:01:19.646
start of development.
